#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jackie Braun|chapter=Most Focused|title=Mr. Right There All Along|series=Harlequin Romance, #4258; The Fun Factor|location=Toronto, Ont.|publisher=[[w:Harlequin Enterprises|Harlequin]]|year=2011|page=220|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/mrrighttherealla0000brau/page/220/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-373-74117-5|passage=And she’d slathered a heavy layer of foundation over the raw skin of her face with the end result being a complexion that was more '''tomato''' than orange.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jillian Cantor|title=Margot|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Riverhead Books|year=2013|pages=[https://archive.org/details/margot0000cant_s1j4/page/93/mode/1up 93–94] (chapter 16) and [https://archive.org/details/margot0000cant_s1j4/page/164/mode/1up 164] (chapter 26)|isbn=978-1-59448-643-2|passage=This afternoon, though, she saunters in, draped in a dress the color of a ripe tomato, with a hat to match, her hair twisted underneath in some kind of fashionable up-do that seems impossible to create oneself. {{...}} Penny is sitting there, on the bed, next to me, chewing on the end of the pen, dressed in her frivolous '''tomato''' dress.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Traci Andrighetti|chapter=9|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-ypeEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT130|title=Valpolicella Violet|series=Franki Amato Mysteries|seriesvolume=7|publisher=Limoncello Press|year=2021|isbn=978-1-7355761-9-0|passage=Intending to tease out Shona’s know-it-all nature by spouting off some trivia, I googled the Pala d’Oro on my phone. It was pure folly, but I was kind of worried about her. “Wikipedia says the cloth has a hundred and eighty-seven enamel plaques depicting Christ and the saints that are decorated with gold, silver, and around two thousand gems.” I peeked at Shona, whose face was '''tomato''', and continued.}}

